        <exercises xml:id="exercises-three-set-venn-diagrams">
            <exercise xml:id="ex-place-twenty-three-sets">
                <statement><p><m>\xi = \{1, 2, \ldots, 20\}</m>, <m>P</m> is the set of factors of <m>20</m>, <m>Q</m> the set of square numbers and <m>R</m> the set of multiples of <m>4</m> in <m>\xi</m>. Place the numbers in a three-set diagram, with <m>P</m>, <m>Q</m>, <m>R</m> in the places of <m>A</m>, <m>B</m>, <m>C</m>.</p></statement>
                <answer><p>Region <m>1</m> <m>\{2, 5, 10\}</m>; <m>2</m> <m>\{1\}</m>; <m>3</m> <m>\{9\}</m>; <m>4</m> <m>\{20\}</m>; <m>5</m> <m>\{4\}</m>; <m>6</m> <m>\{16\}</m>; <m>7</m> <m>\{8, 12\}</m>; <m>8</m> <m>\{3, 6, 7, 11, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18, 19\}</m></p></answer>
            </exercise>
            <exercise xml:id="ex-words-to-regions">
                <statement><p>Give the region numbers of the elements (a) in <m>A</m> only; (b) in <m>B</m> and <m>C</m> but not <m>A</m>; (c) in at least one of <m>A</m> and <m>B</m>.</p></statement>
                <answer><p>(a) <m>\{1\}</m> (b) <m>\{6\}</m> (c) <m>\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\}</m></p></answer>
            </exercise>
            <exercise xml:id="ex-radio-tv-phone">
                <statement><p>In a survey of <m>80</m> households in Kakamega, <m>52</m> have a radio, <m>30</m> a television and <m>41</m> a smartphone; <m>18</m> have a radio and a television, <m>24</m> a radio and a smartphone, and <m>14</m> a television and a smartphone; <m>9</m> have all three. How many have a radio only? Exactly two of the three? None of them?</p></statement>
                <answer><p>Radio only <m>19</m>; exactly two <m>29</m>; none <m>4</m></p></answer>
                <solution><p>Centre <m>9</m>. Exactly two: <m>18 - 9 = 9</m>, <m>24 - 9 = 15</m>, <m>14 - 9 = 5</m>, total <m>29</m>. Only: radio <m>52 - 9 - 15 - 9 = 19</m>, television <m>30 - 9 - 5 - 9 = 7</m>, smartphone <m>41 - 15 - 5 - 9 = 12</m>. Inner regions <m>19 + 7 + 12 + 29 + 9 = 76</m>, so none <m>= 80 - 76 = 4</m>.</p></solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise xml:id="ex-reading-radio-tv-phone">
                <statement><p>In <xref ref="ex-radio-tv-phone"/>, how many households have at least two of the three? Exactly one?</p></statement>
                <answer><p>At least two <m>38</m>; exactly one <m>38</m></p></answer>
            </exercise>
            <exercise xml:id="ex-why-centre-first">
                <statement><p>Explain why the centre must be filled before the <q>exactly two</q> regions.</p></statement>
                <answer><p>Each pair total includes the people in all three sets, so the centre must be known before it can be taken away from each pair total.</p></answer>
            </exercise>
        </exercises>

        <exercises xml:id="exercises-three-set-challenge" component="core">
            <title>Challenge for Core</title>
            <exercise xml:id="ex-three-set-formula-check">
                <statement><p>Check your answer to <xref ref="ex-radio-tv-phone"/> with the formula for <m>n(A \cup B \cup C)</m>.</p></statement>
                <answer><p><m>52 + 30 + 41 - 18 - 24 - 14 + 9 = 76 = 80 - 4</m></p></answer>
            </exercise>
        </exercises>

        <axiom component="lesson-plan">
            <title>Differentiation</title>
            <table xml:id="table-differentiation-three-set-venn-diagrams">
                <title>Differentiation Strategies</title>
                <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                    <row header="yes" bottom="medium"><cell>Learner Group</cell><cell>Strategy and Learning Experience</cell></row>
                    <row><cell>Struggling Learners (Support)</cell><cell>Work through the activity and <xref ref="example-crops-in-bungoma"/> with a card listing the five steps. Assign <xref ref="ex-place-twenty-three-sets"/> and <xref ref="ex-radio-tv-phone"/>.</cell></row>
                    <row><cell>On-Level Learners (Core)</cell><cell>Full activity and all examples. Assign all the exercises.</cell></row>
                    <row><cell>Advanced Learners (Challenge)</cell><cell>All exercises. Extension: make up totals for a three-set survey of <m>50</m> people that give a negative region. What does that tell you about the survey?</cell></row>
                </tabular>
            </table>
        </axiom>

